  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nThe Latin small letter ß has a named entity `&szlig;` The capital version ẞ is currently missing a named entity.\n\nFor consistency I propose to add the named entity `&Szlig;`\n\nAccording to DIN 5008:2020, when using capital letters, the capital ẞ is preferable to the resolution in SS or SZ.\n\nEven though ẞ is rarely used in formulas, this should also be synchronized with MathML: https://w3c.github.io/xml-entities/\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nA workaround would be using `&#7838;` or `&#x1E9E;` which are not intuitive. Because `&szlig;` already exists for the lowercase letter, `&Szlig;` would be the logical conclusion for the uppercase letter.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Anything else?\n\nUnlike ß, ẞ is not available on many keyboard layouts and also not part of the common Windows-1252 encoding (also known as Latin-1), so it is important to have an entity to comply with DIN 5008:2020 and the official spelling rules for the locales de_DE, de_AT, de_BE, de_IT and de_LU.",
